KeyPrism — third-party license inventory (NOTICE v2, Phase 3.11 final audit)
=============================================================================

KeyPrism is MIT-licensed. This file inventories the licenses of the
third-party dependencies actually shipped/used at this release, so the
obligations stay visible as the dependency set grows. It is generated
by hand against pyproject.toml / frontend/package.json and re-verified
per release (deliberately not automated in CI: the set is small and the
characterizations need judgment, not just a package listing — reviewed
as part of every changelog cut).

Python runtime dependencies (pyproject [project].dependencies)
--------------------------------------------------------------
numpy         BSD-3-Clause
scipy         BSD-3-Clause
matplotlib    BSD-3-Clause (bundled fonts carry their own licenses:
              STIX/BaKoMa/AMSMaMa etc. — redistribution of wheels is
              covered by the matplotlib distribution terms)
mido          MIT
soundfile     BSD-3-Clause (Python package); the libsndfile binary it
              bundles is LGPL-2.1-or-later.
              LGPL notice (resolved 3.11): KeyPrism never bundles or
              modifies libsndfile — the library arrives inside the
              soundfile wheel from PyPI as an unmodified, separately
              linked shared library, which satisfies the LGPL for
              distribution. Any distributor who re-ships those wheels
              must keep this notice (and the library's own LICENSE
              shipped inside the wheel) intact; the LGPL does not
              attach to KeyPrism's MIT code.
av (PyAV)     BSD-3-Clause (Python package); the FFmpeg shared
              libraries bundled in its wheels are LGPL-2.1-or-later
              (default builds).
              LGPL notice (resolved 3.11): same story as libsndfile —
              unmodified FFmpeg shared libraries inside the PyAV wheel,
              dynamically linked, never statically merged into
              KeyPrism. Carry this notice and PyAV's bundled FFmpeg
              LICENSE when redistributing the wheels; no further
              obligation for KeyPrism's own code.

