Models / pretrained weights (not distributed with KeyPrism; downloaded
at first run to ~/.keyprism/models/demucs/)
------------------------------------------------------------------
Demucs code (facebookresearch/demucs)  MIT — both htdemucs variants
              are conversions of this MIT codebase's weights.

htdemucs_6s ONNX (StemSplitio/htdemucs-6s-onnx, the demucs_6
auto-download source):
              MIT — the export repo ships an explicit LICENSE; the
              6-stem registry order (drums/bass/other/vocals/guitar/
              piano) mirrors that export. Weights are auto-downloaded
              from the Hub at first use and NEVER stored in the
              KeyPrism repository; every resolved model file records
              its provenance (repo id, revision, commit, etag, license
              URL, source URL) into <model_dir>/provenance.json for
              exactly this audit.

htdemucs ONNX (smank/htdemucs-onnx, the demucs_4 auto-download
source):
              Demucs code MIT; the community export repo does not
              restate a weight license (dlsep._VARIANTS records
              license "unknown (community export)" plus the repo URL).
              FLAG (carried over from NOTICE v1): the htdemucs weights
              were trained with MUSDB18-HQ and similar sources;
              MUSDB18(-HQ) is released for ACADEMIC / RESEARCH USE
              ONLY. That usage restriction travels with the weights,
              not with KeyPrism's code: KeyPrism does not redistribute
              the weights, and makes no claim about their fitness for
              production/commercial use. Prefer demucs_6 (MIT,
              fully characterized) when licensing matters.

