License compatibility with KeyPrism (MIT)
-----------------------------------------
Core product (default install + [dl] + [dl-directml]): all runtime
dependencies are permissive (MIT / BSD-3-Clause / Apache-2.0 / ISC).
No license conflict for the core MIT product.

Non-OSI components
------------------
The only non-OSI, proprietary components in the dependency tree are
the NVIDIA wheels of the OPTIONAL [dl-cuda] extra (CUDA Toolkit EULA +
cuDNN License Agreement, see above). Consequences, by design:
  - They are opt-in: plain `uv sync`, the `[dl]` extra (CPU
    onnxruntime) and the Windows `[dl-directml]` extra never install
    them; the core MIT product ships none of them.
  - They are Linux-only (pyproject platform markers); other platforms
    never even resolve them.
  - They are fetched by the user's own package manager directly from
    PyPI; KeyPrism does not redistribute, embed or re-host them.
  - Their terms govern those wheels only and do not viralize into
    KeyPrism's MIT code (no source obligations; NVIDIA's pip wheels
    are published for exactly this redistribution).
The core product remains MIT-clean; the GPU acceleration extras are
flagged proprietary for anyone auditing a deployment that enables them.

Known obligations to track (none blocking):
  - LGPL-2.1 (libsndfile via soundfile, FFmpeg libs via PyAV wheels):
    keep them unmodified as separately-linked libraries; this NOTICE
    (plus the license files inside the wheels) constitutes the
    required notice for any binary redistribution of those wheels —
    resolved 3.11, no further action.
  - Apache-2.0 (basic-pitch, huggingface-hub, tensorflow): requires
    retaining NOTICE files and stating changes if modified. Compatible
    with MIT distribution; no action beyond this inventory.
  - Research-only weights lineage (MUSDB18-HQ behind the 4-stem
    demucs export): restriction travels with the auto-downloaded
    weights, not with KeyPrism code; documented above, surfaced via
    provenance.json. No further action for this release.
